{"kind":"assert","text":"S1 F1 early note on candidate 821f4ec3, before your review request: the early return in `#close` skips the map cleanup. Fix it before you file.\n\nAt 821f4ec3, `#close` returns `owner.disposed()` for a closed owner before it reaches `done.finally(...)`. That `finally` is the only place that removes the layer from `#layers`. An OAuth generation can close itself: its lifetime timer and `expireIfDue` call `graceful()` directly, with `lifetime.expires` set from the OAuth deadline in hosted.ts line 712. Its layer then stays in `#layers`. On main, every later `#close` of that layer removed the entry. At the candidate, no `#close` path removes it, so only `open()` for the same grant id (by overwriting the entry) or `abrupt()` clears it.\n\nProbe, outside your worktree, on main c85553da and on the candidate's packages/mcp/src, with esbuild from the shared node_modules and stub access ports:\n- Eight grants open, all eight generations retire themselves with `graceful()`, the grants stop being current, and a ninth grant opens. Main opens the ninth grant. The candidate returns null, because the eight stale layers still fill `OAUTH_GRANTS_MOST`. `closeGrant` and `closeAll` do not clear them, and the ninth grant stays refused.\n- Detach, then close in the same turn: main ends with `retained` false (the S1 F1 defect), and the candidate ends with `retained` true.\n\nKeep the check inside the `finally` chain:\n\n\tconst done = owner.closed ? owner.disposed()\n\t  : disposition === \"detach\" ? (owner.detach(), Promise.resolve())\n\t  : owner.graceful();\n\nWith that change, the same probe opens the ninth grant, and detach-then-close keeps `retained` true. The `finally` deletes the entry only while `#layers` still holds this exact layer, so a newer layer for the same id stays. A witness for this case would retire a held generation with `graceful()`, make its grant non-current, and show that a new grant still opens.\n\nThe seal at 821f4ec3 is correct: I recomputed oauth-http.ts as 1c87328b… on main and dc4b7c11… at the candidate. The fix changes that literal again. Hosted MCP is closed on all three Workers, so no live path reaches either defect today.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}